-- One encoding, two renderings. `l4 nlg --lang he` and `l4 render --lang he`
-- select the Hebrew one; with no flag, or for a language this file does not
-- carry, the default rendering is used.
--
-- `is small` deliberately has ONLY an English rendering, so that asking for
-- Hebrew exercises the fall-back rather than producing a hole.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is large` @nlg:en the claim of %amount% exceeds the threshold
                  @nlg:he %amount% עולה על הסף
  IF amount GREATER THAN 100

GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is small` @nlg:en the claim of %amount% is under the threshold
  IF amount LESS THAN 10

#EVAL `is large` 150
#EVAL `is small` 5
